`pgvector` is a Postgres extension that adds a native vector column type and similarity search directly to Postgres — which matters concretely for this app: since the whole platform already runs on Supabase/Postgres, pgvector means RAG features need zero extra infrastructure, just a migration adding a `vector` column and an index.

```sql
create extension if not exists vector;
alter table chunks add column embedding vector(1536);
create index on chunks using ivfflat (embedding vector_cosine_ops);

select content from chunks
order by embedding <=> '[0.02,-0.11,...]'
limit 5;
```

For the Healthcare AI Knowledge Assistant build, this is the recommended default over standing up a separate vector service — one less moving part, one less thing to keep in sync with the rest of the app's data.
